  "title": "Harriet Tubman",
  "summary": "Born into slavery on Maryland's Eastern Shore, Tubman escaped and made about 13 trips back into Maryland to bring out family and friends. In June 1863 she joined a Union raid on plantations along the Combahee River that freed more than 700 people. She bought a house in Auburn, New York, in 1859 and died there in 1913.",
